# Tabulated three-body recombination for react table.
#
# style T: activation energy, energy release, then the file and section
# keyword holding the recombination cross section.
#
# A recombination reaction is three-body, so its probability carries the
# number density n3 of the third particle SPARTA picks from the same grid
# cell:
#
#   P_react = n3 * sigma_rec(E) / sigma_total(E)
#
# sigma_rec is therefore a cross section per unit third-body number
# density, tabulated in m^5, so that <sigma_rec*g> is the ordinary
# three-body rate coefficient in m^6/s.
#
# Writing the reaction with a single product leaves the third body
# unspecified, so any species can act as it.  Naming a species as a second
# product instead restricts the reaction to that third body.

O + O --> O2
R T 0.0 8.197e-19 recomb.tab O2_RECOMB
